A Complete Faith (18-23);
The Heart of the Matter (24);
Powerful Analogy (25-26)

Exodus 19 has been referred to as the most influential chapter of the entire Bible.
Setting: 19:1-3a; 
Preamble and Prologue: 3b-4 (Deut 29:2-3); 
Promises and Conditions: 5-6; 
"On eagle's wings" (Deut 32:9-11); 
"Treasured possession" (1 Chron 29:1-3); 
Kingdom of Priests: 6; 
Holy Nation: 6; 
Condition: 5; 
What is our calling? (1 Pet 2:1-12)

This is about our story of salvation. 1 Corinthians 10:11; Luke 9:28-31.
I. Powerful enemy - v. 1-9;
II. Palpable Fear - v. 10-12;
III. Omnipotent Savior - v. 13-14; Colossians 2:13-15; 1 Cor 1:18-31; Romans 5:6-8

I. Having “God's Laws Written on Our Hearts” is [Simply] a Definition of True Holiness.

II. In The New Covenant, God Has Made Glorious Provision for Your Holiness.

III. Notwithstanding God's Wonderful Provision, We Must Exert Ourselves in Pursuing Holiness By…

1. Looking, in faith, to Jesus Christ through His Holy Spirit as our essential and all-sufficient source of grace and power for holiness.

2. Using the [public and private] means of grace faithfully.

3. Guarding our hearts diligently;

4. Avoiding temptation whenever we can;

5. Resisting temptation when we can't avoid it;

6. Repenting of our sins, looking to Christ for forgiveness, and confessing our sins to God and men;

7. Mortifying the deeds of the flesh;

8.  Resisting the Devil;

9. Cultivating godly company;

10. “Improving” our afflictions.

Four Lessons to learn:
1) No matter how spiritual we may be, we can fall into error, just look at the Apostle Peter;
2) We can influence others by our behavior, others were influenced by Peter even Barnabas;
3) We all need a Paul to get us back on track, the Apostle Peter needed Paul and we need other saints who see when we are actng out of line with the Gospel and will confront us and bring us back;
4) We must confront one another in an atmosphere of mutual respect in the sight of God. Paul honored Peter and the great working of God in his ministry. Peter in 2Peter 3 honors Paul and the wisdom God has given him. We need to confront one another in the spirit of love and mutual respect.
